# ============================================================================
# log_agent.py - Exclude patterns (silence log lines)
# ============================================================================
# Lines in this file are filtered out: they trigger neither an AI analysis
# nor a Pushover alert. The file is re-read on every run - no restart needed.
#
# Format:
#   - One regex per line, case-insensitive.
#   - Lines starting with '#' are comments. Blank lines are ignored.
#   - A pattern without a prefix applies to ALL log sources.
#   - A prefix 'source:' limits the pattern to one source. The source name is
#     the file name without the path, e.g. 'syslog' or 'auth.log'.
#   - The prefix '*:' means all sources (same as no prefix).
#
# Examples:
#
#   # Silence all lines containing 'networkd-dispatcher' in any source:
#   networkd-dispatcher
#
#   # Silence only in auth.log:
#   auth.log:^sudo:.*incorrect password
#
#   # Silence a specific service in syslog (note that ':' works in a regex):
#   syslog:^kernel:.*\[nfc\]
# ============================================================================

# Own root logins (sshd) via "Accepted publickey" from 192.0.2.10.
# Silence only in auth.log, where the "accepted publickey" pattern triggers.
auth.log:Accepted publickey for root from 192.0.2.10
auth.log:Accepted publickey for root from 192.0.2.159